WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.070
A photo posted to Marvel Studios' Instagram
and Twitter accounts featuring most of the

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.760
MCU's female characters on the set of Avengers:
Endgame has stoked the ire of fans.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.380
Why?

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.580
Well, not for who it does include, but for
who it doesn't.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.700
Along with a few key crew members, the black-and-white
photo features the vast majority of the MCU's

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:23.910
women posing and smiling for the camera, including
Danai Gurira as Okoye, Elizabeth Olsen as

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.910
Scarlet Witch, Gwyneth Paltrow as Pepper Potts,
Brie Larson as Captain Marvel, Evangeline

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:34.800
Lilly as the Wasp, Letitia Wright as Shuri,
Pom Klementieff as Mantis, Zoe Saldana as

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.240
Gamora, and Karen Gillan as Nebula.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:42.060
But Scarlett Johansson's Black Widow and Tessa
Thompson's Valkyrie are missing in action.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.580
There is, of course, a good reason for this.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.360
Due to scheduling conflicts, Thompson's Valkyrie
had to be digitally inserted into her scenes

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:54.670
during Endgame's climactic battle — meaning
that she wasn't excluded, simply unavailable.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.080
As for Black Widow… well, spoiler alert...

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.240
Black Widow took a swan dive off a cliff on
the alien planet of Vormir.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.480
The good news is that she managed to retrieve
the Soul Stone for Jeremy Renner's Hawkeye.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:09.560
The bad news is that the character bit the
big one, and couldn't join in the big fight

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.100
against Thanos during the movie's climax.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.780
This being the case, there was obviously no
earthly reason for Johansson to be on set

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.460
the day that this photo was taken.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:22.620
As you can plainly see, the cast and crew
were in the midst of shooting that big final

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.200
battle, by which point Johansson's contribution
to the film was complete.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.950
Sure, somebody could have given her a ring
and invited her to come on back down to the

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.760
set to pose for this lovely shot with her
castmates.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:37.880
But we're talking about a world-famous A-list
actress who just might have had another professional

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.340
engagement on the day that they decided to
snap an impromptu photo.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.820
Of course, knowing this didn't keep fans on
social media from completely losing their

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.560
minds over the totally understandable exclusions.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.060
Complicating matters is the fact that many
fans have widely speculated that the all-female

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:57.570
team-up scene in Endgame was also meant to
tease the imminent arrival of a movie based

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:03.720
on A-Force, a team of superpowered women introduced
in the pages of Marvel comics in 2016.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.620
One fan even promised an uprising if Black
Widow were to be excluded from such a project,

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.940
should it ever actually materialize, tweeting:

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.700
"I swear to god if the A-Force movie is made
without Natalia Alianovna Romanova WE RIOT!!!!"

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.760
That, of course, completely disregards the
fact that the character is, you know, dead,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.380
and that her forthcoming solo film is pretty
much guaranteed to be a prequel.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.500
And to say that this was the only such tweet
to light up the internet as a result of this

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.400
photo would be an understatement.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.660
Of course, for every fan ready to burn down
the internet over their favorite lady Avengers

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.830
being missing from the shot, there was at
least one more jumping in to helpfully point

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.200
out that neither of them were on set that
day.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:47.540
This fact rather than some nefarious, photo-excluding
conspiracy was the likely reason for their

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.200
absence.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.660
But apparently, there simply aren't enough
things in the world for some people to get

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.890
worked up over, which is the only reason we
can think of for there to be any controversy

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.400
of any type whatsoever over this perfectly
charming photo.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.460
For its part, Marvel Studios has not commented
on the kerfuffle, because of course it hasn't.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.100
This is just Twitter being Twitter.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.780
Obviously we're hoping for an A-Force movie
just as hard as everyone else, but let's not

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.360
declare such a project an absolute failure
if it doesn't completely satisfy every single

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.120
member of its intended audience.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.100
Fortunately, Marvel Studios takes its marching
orders but from Kevin Feige [FYE-gee, hard

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.040
G], who has yet to steer the studio wrong.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:23.960
And who knows?

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.640
Maybe an A-Force movie could do the hard work
of tasking its cast of characters with the

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.880
tough job of somehow bringing Black Widow
back to life!

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.220
It worked for Superman in Justice League,
right?

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:38.960
"Do you feel a sense of confidence that we're
not doing something horribly wrong and macabre

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:39.460
here?"

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:40.940
"Not really."

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.060
Uhhhhh...on second thought...never mind.

